From: Switch-CrOS Authors
Subject: [PATCH] shill: ignore auto-created dummy0 / bond0 interfaces

The L4T 4.9 kernel builds CONFIG_DUMMY and CONFIG_BONDING in, so the
kernel auto-creates dummy0 and bond0 at boot.  dummy0 always reports
carrier (LOWER_UP) and has no driver symlink, so shill classifies it as
a connected Ethernet device and runs DHCP on it forever — it never
completes, which keeps a bogus "Ethernet" network perpetually
"connecting" in the UI and jams the network quick-settings panel.

Neither interface is a real network device on the Switch.  Add them to
kIgnoredDeviceNamePrefixes (prefix match, so dummyN/bondN are all
covered) so shill leaves them alone.

--- a/device_info.cc
+++ b/device_info.cc
@@ -152,6 +152,13 @@
     // for now.
     "arc_",
     "veth",
+    // switch-t210: the L4T 4.9 kernel builds the dummy and bonding drivers
+    // in, which auto-create dummy0 and bond0 at boot.  dummy0 always
+    // reports carrier (LOWER_UP), so shill classifies it as a connected
+    // Ethernet device and tries to DHCP on it forever, jamming the network
+    // UI.  Neither is a real device on the Switch; ignore them.
+    "dummy",
+    "bond",
 };
 
 // As of Linux v5.4, these "kinds" are not part of a UAPI header definition, so
